==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|spýja|lang=non}}, from {{proto|Germanic|spīwanan|lang=is}}, whence also German {{term|speien|lang=de}}, Englih ''[[spew]]'', Gothic {{term|𐍃𐍀𐌴𐌹𐍅𐌰𐌽|tr=speiwan|lang=got}}. Non-Germanic cognates include Old Armenian {{term|թուք||tr=tʿukʿ|lang=xcl}}, Persian {{term|تف||spittle|tr=tuf|lang=fa}}, Ossetian {{term|ту||spittle|lang=os}}, Ancient Greek {{term|πτύω||I spit out|tr=ptuō|lang=grc}}, Latin {{term|spuo|lang=la}}, Old Church Slavonic {{term|пльвати||lang=cu}} (Russian {{term|плевать|lang=ru}}) and Sanskrit {{term|ष्ठीवति|tr=ṣṭhīvati||to spit|lang=sa}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈspiːja/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|iːja|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|spjó|spjóu|spúið}} ''or'' {{is-verb-weak|spúði|spúið}}

# to [[vomit]]
# to [[spit]] out, make [[gush]] forth

====Conjugation====
Strong or (increasingly commonly) weak. May also be mixed, with the strong forms being retained mostly in the singular past indicative forms.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|spýju|spýjur}}

# [[vomit]]
# a thick [[shower]] of [[rain]] in windy conditions
# a small [[avalanche]]

